    pharm: "1. First-line (prostaglandin analogue): Latanoprost 0.005% eye drops once daily at night (most effective, once daily, well-tolerated). 2. If IOP not at target after 4-6 weeks, add: Timolol 0.5% (beta-blocker) BID. Or Dorzolamide 2% TID (carbonic anhydrase inhibitor). Or Brimonidine 0.2% BID (alpha-2 agonist). 3. If IOP still elevated: fixed combination drops (e.g., Latanoprost/Timolol) to improve adherence. 4. If maximal medical therapy fails AND IOP remains elevated with progression: Laser Trabeculoplasty (SLT) or Trabeculectomy (surgery). 5. Avoid systemic carbonic anhydrase inhibitors (Acetazolamide) for chronic use (side effects). Reserve for acute IOP elevation.",
